# pf rules for an anchor loaded by knockd (PFCMD), so the car's own AP can reach
# the knock and SSH ports. Deploy as /var/opt/aa/pf.nbtaad.
#
# NOT VERIFIED on the car yet (IMPROVEMENT-PLAN A2 recon: pfctl -s rules,
# pfctl -s Anchors). The stock default is "block drop all"; the filter_OBD anchor
# already passes 851/3804 on dwc0, and uap0's stock pass list does not include
# them. Port numbers must match knock.conf PORT and sshd_config Port.
pass in quick on uap0 proto tcp from any to (uap0) port 851 keep state
pass in quick on uap0 proto tcp from any to (uap0) port 3804 keep state
